00:00:04,199 --> 00:00:06,914
The fountain.

3
00:00:06,915 --> 00:00:13,079
that for 6,000 years, and no one knows how many millions of ages before, the

4
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:17,558
great whale should have been spouting all over the sea, and sprinkling and

5
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:22,518
mystifying the gardens of the deep, as with so many sprinkling or mystifying

6
00:00:22,519 --> 00:00:27,719
pots, and that for some centuries back thousands of hunters should have been

7
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:31,318
close by the fountain of the whale, watching these sprinklings and

8
00:00:31,319 --> 00:00:37,318
spoutings, that all this should be, and yet that down to this blessed minute, 15

9
00:00:37,319 --> 00:00:44,274
and 1/4 minutes past 1:00 p.m. of this 16th day of December AD1 1851.

10
00:00:44,275 --> 00:00:48,755
It should still remain a problem whether these spoutings are after all really

11
00:00:48,756 --> 00:00:55,079
water or nothing but vapor. This is surely a noteworthy thing. Let us then

12
00:00:55,080 --> 00:01:00,115
look at this matter along with some interesting items contingent. Everyone

13
00:01:00,116 --> 00:01:05,159
knows that by the peculiar cunning of their gills, the Finey tribes in general

14
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:09,399
breathe the air which at all times is combined with the element in which they

15
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:15,159
swim. Hence, a herring or cod might live a century and never once raise its head

16
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:19,558
above the surface. But owing to his marked internal structure which gives

17
00:01:19,559 --> 00:01:24,838
him regular lungs like a human being's, the whale can only live by inhaling the

18
00:01:24,839 --> 00:01:28,115
disengaged air in the open atmosphere.

19
00:01:28,116 --> 00:01:32,838
Wherefore the necessity for his periodical visits to the upper world,

20
00:01:32,839 --> 00:01:37,318
but he cannot in any degree breathe through his mouth, for in his ordinary

21
00:01:37,319 --> 00:01:41,878
attitude, the sperm whale's mouth is buried at least 8 ft beneath the

22
00:01:41,879 --> 00:01:46,755
surface. And what is still more, his windpipe has no connection with his

23
00:01:46,756 --> 00:01:54,518
mouth. No, he breathes through his spiracle alone, and this is on the top of his head.

24
00:01:54,519 --> 00:01:59,719
If I say that in any creature breathing is only a function indispensable to

25
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:05,079
vitality, in as much as it withdraws from the air a certain element, which

26
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:09,719
being subsequently brought into contact with the blood, imparts to the blood its

27
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:15,479
vivifying principle, I do not think I shall heir, though I may possibly use

28
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,359
some superfluous scientific words.

29
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:22,755
Assume it, and it follows that if all the blood in a man could be airrated in

30
00:02:22,756 --> 00:02:27,399
one breath, he might then seal up his nostrils and not fetch another for a

31
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:33,479
considerable time. That is to say, he would then live without breathing.

32
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:37,795
Anomalous as it may seem, this is precisely the case with the whale, who

33
00:02:37,796 --> 00:02:42,755
systematically lives by intervals his full hour and more, when at the bottom,

34
00:02:42,756 --> 00:02:47,638
without drawing a single breath, or so much as in any way inhaling a particle

35
00:02:47,639 --> 00:02:51,159
of air, or remember, he has no gills.

36
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:56,274
How is this? Between his ribs and on each side of his spine, he is supplied

37
00:02:56,275 --> 00:03:01,638
with a remarkable involved labyrinth of vermicelli-like vessels,

38
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:05,719
which vessels, when he quits the surface, are completely distended with

39
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:11,795
oxygenated blood, so that for an hour or more a thousand fathoms in the sea, he

40
00:03:11,796 --> 00:03:17,079
carries a surplus stock of vitality in him, just as the camel crossing the

41
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:21,795
waterless desert carries a surplus supply of drink for future use in its

42
00:03:21,796 --> 00:03:26,999
force. for supplementary stomachs. The anatomical fact of this labyrinth is

43
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:32,518
indisputable, and that the supposition founded upon it is reasonable and true,

44
00:03:32,519 --> 00:03:37,159
seems the more cogent to me when I consider the otherwise inexplicable

45
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:42,039
obstinacy of that Leviathan in having his spoutings out, as the fishermen

46
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:47,795
phrase it. This is what I mean. If unmolested upon rising to the surface,

47
00:03:47,796 --> 00:03:52,518
the sperm whale will continue there for a period of time exactly uniform with

48
00:03:52,519 --> 00:03:59,479
all his other unmolested risings. Say he stays 11 minutes and jets 70 times, that

49
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:05,318
is respires 70 breaths, then whenever he rises again, he will be sure to have his

50
00:04:05,319 --> 00:04:08,755
70 breaths all over again to a minute.

51
00:04:08,756 --> 00:04:14,435
Now, if after he fetches a few breaths, you alarm him so that he sounds, he will

52
00:04:14,436 --> 00:04:19,719
be always dodging up again to make good his regular allowance of air, and not

53
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:24,518
till those 70 breaths are told will he finally go down to stay out his full

54
00:04:24,519 --> 00:04:29,954
term below. Remark, however, that in different individuals these rates are

55
00:04:29,955 --> 00:04:34,914
different, but in any one they are alike. Now, why should the whale thus

56
00:04:34,915 --> 00:04:39,878
insist upon having his spoutings out, unless it be to replenish his reservoir

57
00:04:39,879 --> 00:04:45,479
of air, air descending for good? How obvious is it, too, that this necessity

58
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:50,914
for the whale's rising exposes him to all the fatal hazards of the chase. For

59
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:55,719
not by hook or by net could this vast leviathan be caught when sailing a

60
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:58,594
thousand fathoms beneath the sunlight.

61
00:04:58,595 --> 00:05:06,435
Not so much thy skill then, oh hunter, as the great necessities that strike the victory to thee.

62
00:05:06,436 --> 00:05:11,878
In man, breathing is incessantly going on, one breath only serving for two or

63
00:05:11,879 --> 00:05:17,079
three pulsations, so that whatever other business he has to attend to, waking or

64
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:22,518
sleeping, breathe he must, or die he will. But the sperm whale only breathes

65
00:05:22,519 --> 00:05:28,435
about 17th or Sunday of his time. It has been said that the whale only breathes

66
00:05:28,436 --> 00:05:32,518
through his spout hole. If it could truthfully be added that his spouts are

67
00:05:32,519 --> 00:05:36,518
mixed with water, then I appine we should be furnished with the reason why

68
00:05:36,519 --> 00:05:41,318
his sense of smell seems obliterated in him. For the only thing about him that

69
00:05:41,319 --> 00:05:46,115
at all answers to his nose is that identical spout hole, and being so

70
00:05:46,116 --> 00:05:50,274
clogged with two elements, it could not be expected to have the power of

71
00:05:50,275 --> 00:05:55,558
smelling. But owing to the mystery of the spout, whether it be water or

72
00:05:55,559 --> 00:06:00,518
whether it be vapor, no absolute certainty can as yet be arrived at on

73
00:06:00,519 --> 00:06:05,238
this head. Sure it is, nevertheless, that the sperm whale has no proper

74
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:13,399
alactories. But what does he want of them? No roses, no violets, no cologne water in the sea.

75
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:18,274
Furthermore, as his windpipe solely opens into the tube of his spouting

76
00:06:18,275 --> 00:06:24,039
canal, and as that long canal, like the Grand Eerie canal, is furnished with a

77
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:29,079
sort of locks that open and shut for the downward retention of air or the upward

78
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:35,079
exclusion of water. Therefore, the whale has no voice, unless you insult him by

79
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:40,115
saying that when he so strangely rumbles, he talks through his nose. But

80
00:06:40,116 --> 00:06:42,679
then again, what has the whale to say?

81
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:47,558
Seldom have I known any profound being that had anything to say to this world,

82
00:06:47,559 --> 00:06:52,679
unless forced to stammer out something by way of getting a living. Oh, happy

83
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:56,679
that the world is such an excellent listener.

84
00:06:56,680 --> 00:07:01,318
Now, the spouting canal of the sperm whale, chiefly intended, as it is, for

85
00:07:01,319 --> 00:07:06,359
the conveyance of air, and for several feet laid along horizontally just

86
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:11,638
beneath the upper surface of his head, and a little to one side. This curious

87
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:14,679
canal is very much like a gas pipe laid

88
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:17,719
down in a city on one side of a street.

89
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:22,679
But the question returns whether this gas pipe is also a water pipe. In other

90
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:27,079
words, whether the spout of the sperm whale is the mere vapor of the exhaled

91
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:31,795
breath or whether that exhaled breath is mixed with water taken in at the mouth

92
00:07:31,796 --> 00:07:36,838
and discharge through the spiracle. It is certain that the mouth indirectly

93
00:07:36,839 --> 00:07:39,318
communicates with the spouting canal.

94
00:07:39,319 --> 00:07:43,479
But it cannot be proved that this is for the purpose of discharging water through

95
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:48,359
the spiracle, because the greatest necessity for so doing would seem to be

96
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:53,878
when in feeding he accidentally takes in water. But the sperm whale's food is far

97
00:07:53,879 --> 00:07:59,238
beneath the surface, and there he cannot spout even if he would. Besides, if you

98
00:07:59,239 --> 00:08:04,435
regard him very closely and time him with your watch, you will find that when

99
00:08:04,436 --> 00:08:09,399
unmolested, there is an undeviating rhyme between the periods of his jets

100
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:13,399
and the ordinary periods of respiration.

101
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:18,274
But why pester one with all this reasoning on the subject? Speak out. You

102
00:08:18,275 --> 00:08:23,079
have seen him spout. Then declare what the spout is. Can you not tell water

103
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:28,679
from air? My dear sir, in this world it is not so easy to settle these plain

104
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:34,198
things. I have ever found your plain things the naughtiest of all. And as for

105
00:08:34,199 --> 00:08:38,914
this whale spout, you might almost stand in it and yet be undecided as to what it

106
00:08:38,915 --> 00:08:41,238
is precisely.

107
00:08:41,239 --> 00:08:46,594
The central body of it is hidden in the snowy sparkling mist enveloping it. And

108
00:08:46,595 --> 00:08:51,318
how can you certainly tell whether any water falls from it when always when you

109
00:08:51,319 --> 00:08:55,719
are close enough to a whale to get a close view of his spout, he is in a

110
00:08:55,720 --> 00:09:00,914
prodigious commotion, the water cascading all around him? And if at such

111
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:05,399
times you should think that you really perceive drops of moisture in the spout,

112
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:09,795
how do you know that they are not merely condensed from its vapor? Or how do you

113
00:09:09,796 --> 00:09:14,518
know that they are not those identical drops superficially lodged in the spout

114
00:09:14,519 --> 00:09:19,479
hole fisher which is counter sunk into the summit of the whale's head? For even

115
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:24,198
when tranquily swimming through the midday sea in a calm with his elevated

116
00:09:24,199 --> 00:09:28,914
hump sundried as a dramadaries in the desert, even then the whale always

117
00:09:28,915 --> 00:09:34,039
carries a small basin of water on his head, as under a blazing sun you will

118
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:38,198
sometimes see a cavity in a rock filled up with rain.

119
00:09:38,199 --> 00:09:43,079
Nor is it at all prudent for the hunter to be over curious touching the precise

120
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:47,954
nature of the whale spout. It will not do for him to be peering into it and

121
00:09:47,955 --> 00:09:52,435
putting his face in it. You cannot go with your pitcher to this fountain and

122
00:09:52,436 --> 00:09:57,479
fill it and bring it away. For even when coming into slight contact with the

123
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:02,039
outer vapory shreds of the jet, which will often happen, your skin will

124
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:07,558
feverishly smart from the acridness of the thing so touching it. And I know one

125
00:10:07,559 --> 00:10:11,954
who, coming into still closer contact with the spout, whether with some

126
00:10:11,955 --> 00:10:17,238
scientific object in view or otherwise, I cannot say, the skin peeled off from

127
00:10:17,239 --> 00:10:22,518
his cheek and arm. Wherefore among whalemen the spout is deemed poisonous.

128
00:10:22,519 --> 00:10:27,719
They try to evade it. Another thing I have heard it said, and I do not much

129
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:32,115
doubt it, that if the jet is fairly spouted into your eyes, it will blind

130
00:10:32,116 --> 00:10:37,399
you. The wisest thing the investigator can do then, it seems to me, is to let

131
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:40,518
this deadly spout alone.

132
00:10:40,519 --> 00:10:45,638
Still, we can hypothesize, even if we cannot prove and establish. My

133
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:50,679
hypothesis is this, that the spout is nothing but missed, and besides other

134
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:55,159
reasons, to this conclusion I am impelled by considerations touching the

135
00:10:55,160 --> 00:11:00,755
great inherent dignity and sublimity of the sperm whale. I account him no common

136
00:11:00,756 --> 00:11:05,954
shallow being in as much as it is an undisputed fact that he is never found

137
00:11:05,955 --> 00:11:11,558
on soundings or near shores. All other whales sometimes are. He is both

138
00:11:11,559 --> 00:11:16,274
ponderous and profound. And I am convinced that from the heads of all

139
00:11:16,275 --> 00:11:23,079
ponderous profound beings such as Plato, Piro, the devil, Jupiter, Dante, and so

140
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:29,159
on, there always goes up a certain semivvisible steam while in the act of

141
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:34,594
thinking deep thoughts. While composing a little treatise on eternity, I had the

142
00:11:34,595 --> 00:11:40,115
curiosity to place a mirror before me, and he long saw reflected there, a

143
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:45,954
curious involved worming and undulation in the atmosphere over my head, the

144
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:51,558
invariable moisture of my hair, while plunged in deep thought after six cups

145
00:11:51,559 --> 00:11:56,755
of hot tea in my thin shingled attic of an August noon. This seems an additional

146
00:11:56,756 --> 00:12:00,435
argument for the above supposition.

147
00:12:00,436 --> 00:12:06,198
And how nobly it raises our conceit of the mighty misty monster to behold him

148
00:12:06,199 --> 00:12:12,755
solemnly sailing through a calm tropical sea. his vast mild head overhung by a

149
00:12:12,756 --> 00:12:18,359
canopy of vapor, engendered by his incommunicable contemplations, and that

150
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:23,079
vapor, as you will sometimes see it, glorified by a rainbow, as if heaven

151
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:28,518
itself had put its seal upon his thoughts. For do you see, rainbows do

152
00:12:28,519 --> 00:12:34,359
not visit the clear air. They only irradiate vapor. And so through all the

153
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:39,399
thick mists of the dim doubts in my mind, divine intuitions now and then

154
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:46,115
shoot, enkindling my fog with a heavenly ray. And for this I thank God for all

155
00:12:46,116 --> 00:12:53,318
have doubts. Many deny, but doubts or denials. Few along with them have intuitions.

156
00:12:53,319 --> 00:12:58,359
Doubts of all things earthly and intuitions of some things heavenly. This

157
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:03,318
combination makes neither believer nor infidel, but makes a man who regards

158
00:13:03,319 --> 00:13:08,400
them both with equal eye.
